    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full suite is green: **35 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## What I did\n\nIn `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, I added an email-uniqueness check inside the existing email-handling block, mirroring the app's established `telephoneInUse` 409 pattern:\n\n```java\nowner.setEmail(email);\nboolean emailInUse = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()\n    .anyMatch(existing -> existing.getEmail() != null\n        && email.equals(existing.getEmail().toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT)));\nif (emailInUse) {\n    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);\n}\n```\n\nKey points that satisfy the spec:\n- `email` is already the trimmed, lower-cased form (via the existing `normalizeEmail`), so the comparison is case-insensitive as required (\"lower-cased email\").\n- Each existing owner's email is lower-cased before comparison, so a stored mixed-case email still collides.\n- The check only runs when an email is supplied (owners without email are unaffected), and it rejects a duplicate with **HTTP 409 Conflict**.",
